<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Remaclus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died c. 673</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Saint Remaclus, Saint Remacle</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Remaclus was a 7th-century monk and missionary from Aquitaine, first abbot of Solignac and later active as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meuse">Meuse</a> region. With land granted by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigebert-iii">Sigebert III of Austrasia</a> he founded the twin abbeys of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stavelot">Stavelot</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malmedy">Malmedy</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardennes">Ardennes</a> around 650, which grew into an ecclesiastical principality. He is venerated as a saint.</p></div>
